Third-party components
----------------------

Isle - liquid-glass shader math and visual reference
  License: GPL-3.0-or-later
  Source: https://github.com/zickrian/isle
  Sift's GLSL shader is derived from Isle's glass shader math.

nucleo-matcher
  License: MPL-2.0
  Source: https://github.com/helix-editor/nucleo
  Used by siftd for fuzzy file-name matching. The MPL-2.0 source of the
  unmodified crate is available from crates.io and its linked repository.

fend-core
  License: MIT
  Source: https://github.com/printfn/fend
  Used by siftd for arithmetic and unit-expression evaluation.

Other Rust dependencies
-----------------------

siftd also uses the `ignore`, `notify`, `serde`, `serde_json`, `toml`, `zbus`,
and `tokio` crates, plus `tempfile` for tests. Their exact versions are pinned
in `daemon/Cargo.lock`; each crate's license is recorded in its crates.io
metadata and source distribution. All are permissive licenses compatible with
GPL-3.0-or-later.

Runtime dependencies
--------------------

GNOME Shell, GJS, GLib, and Mutter are provided by the operating system and are
not distributed with Sift. GNOME Shell is GPL-2.0-or-later; GJS, GLib, and
Mutter are LGPL-2.1-or-later. Sift uses their public extension APIs at runtime.
